# Runtime settings for /root/deploy/redactplus-landing/app.env (mode 600, root-owned).
# Names and placeholders only. Every value here is read at request time, so changing
# one needs `docker compose up -d` (a container restart), not a new image.
#
# Integrations stay off until each has its own approved RedactPlus values. Never reuse
# the SafariDesk, saferedact.io or Netlify-production values for this deployment.

# --- Reverse proxy ---
# Host nginx is the only hop and overwrites X-Forwarded-For with the client address,
# so exactly one trusted hop. Used for contact-form rate limiting.
TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=1

# --- CMS (Decap at /admin) ---
# Off for this deployment: /admin/config.yml serves the disabled profile (.invalid
# origins), so the editor cannot authenticate.
CMS_ENABLED=false

# --- Support chat (Chatwoot) ---
# Off unless a dedicated RedactPlus inbox is approved. All three must be valid to enable.
OPENREDAKT_CHATWOOT_ENABLED=false
# OPENREDAKT_CHATWOOT_BASE_URL=https://replace-with-the-dedicated-chatwoot-origin
# OPENREDAKT_CHATWOOT_WEBSITE_TOKEN=replace-with-the-public-website-token

# --- Sales and contact enquiries (/api/contact) ---
# Unset: forms validate and tell the visitor nothing was delivered.
# To deliver through SpaceMail, set ALL of the following together (see
# docs/operations/enquiry-email.md). Host, port and security are Spaceship's published
# SpaceMail settings; re-check them in the SpaceMail panel before go-live.
# LEAD_DELIVERY_SMTP_HOST=mail.spacemail.com
# LEAD_DELIVERY_SMTP_PORT=465
# LEAD_DELIVERY_SMTP_SECURITY=tls
# LEAD_DELIVERY_SMTP_USER=no-reply@redactplus.io
# LEAD_DELIVERY_SMTP_PASSWORD=replace-with-the-mailbox-password
# LEAD_DELIVERY_FROM=no-reply@redactplus.io
# LEAD_DELIVERY_FROM_NAME=RedactPlus Website
# LEAD_DELIVERY_TO=support@redactplus.io
# Optional: send sales enquiries (sales form, or a package chosen) somewhere else.
# LEAD_DELIVERY_SALES_TO=replace-with-the-sales-mailbox
# LEAD_DELIVERY_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
#
# The HTTPS-API transport (LEAD_DELIVERY_ENDPOINT, LEAD_DELIVERY_TOKEN) is the
# alternative. Never set both.

# --- Trial registration (/api/registration) ---
# Required in production: registration is a permanent part of the Download dialog. Until these are
# set the form answers "account creation isn't available right now" and creates nothing, and the
# server-side deploy command refuses (rolls back) a release whose registration is not configured.
# The image is built with NEXT_PUBLIC_PORTAL_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY (build-image.sh).
# The endpoint takes no API credential; the forwarder token only proves to the Control Center that
# the visitor address this server forwards is genuine. It is the same value as the API's
# TRIAL_FORWARDER_TOKEN (generate once: openssl rand -hex 32). Keep it out of logs, tickets and chat.
# REDACTPLUS_REGISTRATION_MODE is left unset (it means the Control Center; demo is next dev only).
# REDACTPLUS_REGISTRATION_API_URL=https://api.saferedact.io/public/trial-registrations
# REDACTPLUS_REGISTRATION_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# REDACTPLUS_REGISTRATION_FORWARDER_TOKEN=replace-with-the-shared-64-hex-character-secret

# --- Blog comments and moderation ---
# Leave unset: comments are refused rather than accepted into nowhere.
# COMMENTS_DATABASE_URL=replace-with-postgres-connection-url
# COMMENTS_DATABASE_SSL=true
# COMMENTS_ABUSE_SECRET=replace-with-a-fresh-32-byte-base64url-key
# COMMENTS_STAFF_GITHUB_USER_IDS=replace-with-numeric-staff-ids
# CMS_GITHUB_REPOSITORY=Safe-Redact/Marketing-Site

# Build-time values do NOT belong here: NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCUMENTATION_URL and SITE_NOINDEX
# are fixed into the image when it is built (see README.md).
